# Build context for engine/Dockerfile.
#
# Without this file `docker build` ships the whole directory, including the
# locally produced 14 MB binary in bin/ and every test artefact. None of it is
# used: the Dockerfile compiles /engine from source in its own stage.

# Compiled binary and runtime artefacts: the image builds its own /engine.
bin/

# Test-only Go files stay in the context on purpose - `go test ./...` is not
# part of the image build, but leaving them out would silently change what
# `docker build` type-checks. They are small, so only caches are dropped.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Never ship a CA private key into an image, in any form.
data/
*.key
*.pem
*.crt

# Local editor and OS noise.
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.log
